-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Quazatron
  Publisher   Hewson, 1986
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Quazatron (1986)(Hewson Consultants)[aka Ziggurat].z80
  MD5         ac51eb58af87fdac9c0c7077db98c90a

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Colour, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The monochrome decks in colour: floors, walls, ramps, arrow
              panels, objects and pads each in their own tone, taken from the
              deck's own colour; every droid painted by its parts as a
              hardware sprite, the player's droid included. The panel below
              the play area is unchanged. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.2: droids in front of and behind each other as in the original
              (v1.2's drafts drew them the wrong way round); no black strips
              from new scenery at the view's edge; Centred view's pace; droids
              and shots glide in Centred view; fewer missed interrupts; the
              Space also fires option. 1.1: Centred view toggle. 1.0: colour
              scenery and painted sprites, Smooth scrolling, the original's
              pace kept by a pace limiter

  Note        Controls: choose 2 on CONTROL SELECTION for the cursor keys
              (fire 0), or 4 for a Kempston joystick. Space also fires (off by
              default): with 2, SPACE fires too. Colour (the Enhanced colours
              line): on, the colour game; off, the game's own picture. Smooth
              scrolling (off by default) glides the view. Centred view (off by
              default; turns Smooth scrolling on) keeps your droid mid-screen,
              about 0.12 s behind; other droids and shots glide between the
              game's updates. It changes the game: the view decides which
              droids move. P pauses; fire resumes. Known issues: in Centred
              view a few pixels at the edge of the play area can show, for
              some frames, what the game never drew there (the void's colour,
              or scenery from elsewhere, sometimes black), in about 1 frame in
              18 in the simulator; Centred view runs about 1.3% slower than
              the original in long scrolling (measured before this version's
              display changes); on fast diagonal walks its view can jump up to
              6 px in a frame; with a lot of sound a few more interrupts are
              missed than in the original. Missing: an even update rhythm, so
              the camera still wobbles 0.6-1.5 px on steady walks; the play
              area's edges in Centred view drawn ahead of the camera. JNext
              only; hardware untested.

