-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      1.0 played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06: approved; 1.1
              (Centred view) approved; 1.2 played by the owner in JNext
              2026-11-06: approved

  Replay      Game state IDENTICAL in 43 runs: v1.0's 6 recordings in 4
              states, 4 bot recordings against the Centred reference game in 4
              states, 3 with Space also fires; no register or memory
              difference at any hook. 88,174,592 canvas pixels equal to the
              colour model at 2,266 commits; 114,583 sprite groups equal to
              their records; 99,689 frames locked; the camera filter model
              equal in 34,281 frames. Depth: at every update the sprites the
              Next shows equal the game's own drawing order (632,321
              overlapping pixels). Display, every frame: every shown play-area
              pixel comes from a committed view in all states but Centred
              view; in Centred view 821 of 14,765 frames still show a few
              pixels no view drew for that place (v1.2 before this round:
              36%). Negatives detected (16), new: the sprite priority of v1.2

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless, v2.09 card read-only: an 8-direction
              Centred walk captured every frame (1,480 frames); option 2 with
              the arrow keys, SPACE and 0 firing; option 4 with a joystick
              (keys ignored); earlier sessions' soaks and flicker runs not
              repeated

  Coverage    v1.0's coverage, plus the Centred reference: 4 bot recordings
              toward every side of the deck, scrolls in all four directions,
              deck edges, deck changes and deaths (r8: no cheats); not
              reached: lifts, the transfer game, later decks

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
